# 11. CONTENT LIFECYCLE AND REDIRECTS

The new architecture must handle changes to published content correctly.

## 11.1 New Article

When an article is published:

- Generate its static HTML.
- Include it in the correct listing.
- Generate SEO metadata.
- Generate JSON-LD.
- Include it in the sitemap.

## 11.2 Updated Article

When an article is updated:

- Regenerate the article HTML.
- Update modification metadata.
- Update structured data.
- Update the sitemap modification date where appropriate.

## 11.3 Unpublished or Deleted Article

When an article is unpublished or deleted:

- Remove its generated HTML.
- Remove it from the listing.
- Remove it from the sitemap.
- Ensure the old URL no longer returns the previous article.

## 11.4 Changed Slug

When a published article's slug changes:

- Generate the new URL.
- Remove the old generated page.
- Update the canonical URL.
- Update sitemap entries.
- Update internal links where practical.
- Create a permanent redirect from the old URL where supported.

Verify Wasmer's redirect capabilities before choosing an implementation.

Do not silently discard old URLs that may already have been indexed.

