Do not rewrite unrelated parts of the application.

Only make changes necessary for the target architecture.

## Rule 6 — No Assumed Infrastructure

Inspect the actual Wasmer and GitHub configuration before changing deployment behavior.

## Rule 7 — No Secret Exposure

Keep credentials in the appropriate secure environment.

## Rule 8 — Validate Every Phase

After completing each phase, run the relevant tests before proceeding.

## Rule 9 — Explain Significant Changes

For each implementation phase, report:

- Files created.
- Files modified.
- Database changes.
- Dependencies added.
- Configuration changes.
- Tests performed.
- Outstanding issues.

## Rule 10 — Do Not Claim Untested Success

Clearly distinguish between:

- Implemented.
- Tested locally.
- Tested in staging.
- Deployed.
- Verified in production.

Do not claim successful deployment or production verification if the required credentials or infrastructure access are unavailable.

## Rule 11 — Handle Limitations Transparently

If the existing Wasmer environment cannot support a required routing behavior, or if a Supabase or GitHub integration cannot be completed due to permissions, explain the exact limitation and provide the least disruptive solution.

Do not silently substitute a different architecture.

## Rule 12 — Do Not Invent Existing Project Details

Use actual code, schema, configuration, and tool results.

Do not assume filenames, table names, database columns, route definitions, or deployment commands.

